# TypeScript

- Use strict TypeScript.
- Never use `any` unless absolutely unavoidable.
- Prefer explicit domain types.
- Avoid unnecessary type assertions.
- Avoid non-null assertions.
- Handle null and undefined explicitly.
- Do not duplicate types.
- Keep domain models independent from UI components.
- Use interfaces for domain models when appropriate.
- Use type aliases for unions and utility types.
- Prefer discriminated unions for tool and state variants.
- Export types explicitly when they are part of a module contract.